From: Surface RT bring-up
Subject: [PATCH 18] grate: track BO uses and drain draws at synchronization boundaries

Replace patch 0006's per-draw CPU wait with per-BO last-use fences.
Same-channel work stays ordered; cross-channel uses and CPU maps wait
for prior work. Retain BO references until the channel drains so queued
GEM handles cannot be recycled. Drain at context flush and channel close,
and after 128 submissions to bound the outstanding queue. Wait before
resource export and flush_resource as presentation/sharing boundaries.

This keeps context flush synchronous and returns no outstanding pipe
fence. It does not implement native fence FDs or asynchronous presentation.
The classic interface's per-context job counter is the fence source.

Applies after 0017. See docs/data/gpu/mesa-0018 for hardware validation.

--- a/src/gallium/drivers/grate/drm/channel.c
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/grate/drm/channel.c
@@ -120,8 +120,30 @@
         return -ENOTSUP;
     }
 
+    util_dynarray_init(&channel->pending_bos, NULL);
     *channelp = channel;
 
+    return 0;
+}
+
+/* Complete all submitted work before presentation, channel close, or a bounded
+ * queue rollover. Retaining BOs prevents GEM handle reuse while jobs are queued.
+ */
+int drm_tegra_channel_drain(struct drm_tegra_channel *channel)
+{
+    if (!channel->pending_jobs)
+        return 0;
+    int err = drm_tegra_fence_wait(&channel->pending, 1000000000UL);
+    if (err)
+        return err;
+    util_dynarray_foreach(&channel->pending_bos, struct grate_bo *, item) {
+        struct grate_bo *bo = *item;
+        if (bo->pending_channel == channel)
+            bo->pending_channel = NULL;
+        grate_bo_unref(bo);
+    }
+    util_dynarray_clear(&channel->pending_bos);
+    channel->pending_jobs = 0;
     return 0;
 }
 
